OUTPUT STRUCTURE INSTRUCTIONS:
- `semantic_write`: record only new, durable or operationally important information.
- `personal_facts`: children, pets, city, stable life circumstances.
- `relationship_hooks`: small things that can naturally open a conversation.
- `upcoming_events`: presentations, interviews, demos, deadlines, high-stakes meetings.
- `work_situations`: real work situations, stakeholders and contexts in which the language is used.
- `preferences`: preferences regarding feedback, working style and pace.
- `confidence_blockers`: stressors, blockers, things that undermine fluency.
- `motivation_drivers`: reasons the learner genuinely cares.
- `vocabulary_targets`: words or vocabulary areas worth practicing further.
- `tone_targets`: how the user wants to sound, e.g. calm, executive, natural.
- `recurring_weaknesses`: recurring communication or language weaknesses, if already apparent.
- Do not record momentary emotions, small talk or guesses.
- `core_guardrail_used`: set to true if the reply declined to provide a ready-made solution, mitigated a risk or steered back to the rules.
- `core_guardrail_reason`: briefly name which rule was applied.